 on the cross that was placed in the foundations of the temple. The global founded in great depth and mounted on wooden beams took its current form in 1838. Its rood screen is a work of outstanding quality, as is the pulpit and the bishop's throne. Has a close relationship with the Jerusalem Patriarchate because ","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Samos","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/M._Timiou_Stavrou._-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-M._Timiou_Stavrou._-_panoramio.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/M._Timiou_Stavrou._-_panoramio.jpg/500px-M._Timiou_Stavrou._-_panoramio.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Bob&Anne Powell","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M._Timiou_Stavrou._-_panoramio.jpg"}},{"id":"samos_wv_tsamadou","areaId":"samos","name":"Tsamadou","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":37.78585,"lng":26.87279},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"samos_wv_tsamadou","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":2,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-23"},"hashtags":["tsamadou","samos"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"It is a pebble beach about 400 m long with turquoise and crystal clear water that deepens abruptly. When northern winds blow high waves are created. It is one of the most beautiful beaches of the island, where few nudists gather mostly on the right side. It is organized with umbrellas and sun loungers. There are tavernas and beach bars along the beach.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Samos","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Lemonakia_Strand_auf_Samos.JPG/1280px-Lemonakia_Strand_auf_Samos.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Lemonakia_Strand_auf_Samos.JPG/500px-Lemonakia_Strand_auf_Samos.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"SchusterNorbert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lemonakia_Strand_auf_Samos.JPG"}},{"id":"samos_wv_lemonakia","areaId":"samos","name":"Lemonakia","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":37.78254,"lng":26.87666},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"samos_wv_lemonakia","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-23"},"hashtags":["lemonakia","samos"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"The beach is about 400 m long with clear waters. When northern winds blow high waves are created. The beach is well organized with sun beds and umbrellas. There is a taverna next to the sea and rooms to let near the beach.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Samos","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Lemonakia_Beach%2C_Samos.jpg/1280px-Lemonakia_Beach%2C_Samos.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Lemonakia_Beach%2C_Samos.jpg/500px-Lemonakia_Beach%2C_Samos.jpg","w":1200,"h":540,"author":"Virreoh","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lemonakia_Beach,_Samos.jpg"}},{"id":"samos_wv_tsabou","areaId":"samos","name":"Tsabou","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":37.80233,"lng":26.8546},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"samos_wv_tsabou","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-23"},"hashtags":["tsabou","samos"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"It’s a small beach of 350 m with pebbles, deep and clear water where high waves are created when strong northerly winds blow. Right after there is a smaller secluded beach. The beach is well organized with sun beds and umbrellas and a taverna close to the coast.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:S